  "nl_text": "This database schema, named rschema_0448, is used to store information about a laboratory environment. It consists of nine tables: User, Experimental_Equipment, Experimental_Consumables, Hazardous_Chemicals, Experimental_Course, User_Usage_of_Equipment, User_Purchase_Consumables, User_Purchase_Hazardous_Chemicals, and User_Participation_in_Course.\nThe User table contains information about the users of the laboratory, including their associated unit, password, phone number, role, user ID, and username. The Experimental_Equipment table contains information about the experimental equipment used in the laboratory, including the acquisition time, device category, device ID, device model, device name, manufacturer, and status. The Experimental_Consumables table contains information about the consumables used in the laboratory, including the category, consumable ID, consumable name, inventory quantity, and status. The Hazardous_Chemicals table contains information about the hazardous chemicals used in the laboratory, including the chemical ID, chemical name, inventory quantity, issuance time, and status.\nThe Experimental_Course table contains information about the experimental courses offered in the laboratory, including the class location, class time, course ID, course name, participants, and teacher ID. The User_Usage_of_Equipment table contains information about the usage of experimental equipment by users, including the device ID, usage purpose, usage time, and user ID. The User_Purchase_Consumables table contains information about the purchase of consumables by users, including the consumable ID, purchase time, and user ID. The User_Purchase_Hazardous_Chemicals table contains information about the purchase of hazardous chemicals by users, including the chemical ID, purchase time, and user ID.\nThe User_Participation_in_Course table contains information about the participation of users in experimental courses, including the course ID, experimental course grade, participation status, and user ID. The tables are related to each other through foreign keys, which ensure referential integrity and entity integrity. For example, the User_Usage_of_Equipment table references the Experimental_Equipment table through the device ID, and the User_Purchase_Consumables table references the Experimental_Consumables table through the consumable ID. The User_Participation_in_Course table references the Experimental_Course table through the course ID and the User table through the user ID.\nOverall, this schema provides a comprehensive and structured way to store and manage information about a laboratory environment, including users, equipment, consumables, and courses. It ensures data consistency and integrity through the use of foreign keys, primary keys, and unique constraints.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\n1.User Management:\nManage user information, including user roles (Student, Teacher, Laboratory Administrator, Experimental Center Director Administrator, System Administrator), username, password, phone number, and associated unit.\n2.Experimental Equipment Management:\nEnter and manage the basic information of laboratory equipment, such as equipment name, model, category, manufacturer, status (inactive, in use, active), and acquisition time.\nUsage Records Management: Record the usage of equipment, including usage time, user, and purpose of use.\nCourse Association Management: Associate equipment with specific experimental courses for easier scheduling and management of the equipment.\n3.Laboratory Consumables Management:\nConsumables Management: Perform operations such as archiving, modifying, and querying consumables information. Manage the purchasing, storage, issuance, and return of consumables.\nRecord consumable name, category, inventory quantity, and status. Users can purchase consumables and record the purchase time.\n4.Hazardous Chemicals Management:\nArchive, modify, and query hazardous chemicals information. Manage the purchasing, storage, issuance, and return of hazardous chemicals to ensure safety.\nRecord chemical name, inventory quantity, issuance time, and status.\n5.Experimental Course Management:\nView and manage information for regular experimental courses, including course name, class time, and class location. Each course can have multiple students registered, and each course is assigned a corresponding teacher.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0448.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0448\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `unit` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Experimental_Equipment` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `device_model` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manufacturer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `acquisition_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `device_category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Experimental_Consumables` (\n  `consumable_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `consumable_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`consumable_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Hazardous_Chemicals` (\n  `chemical_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `chemical_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `issuance_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`chemical_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Experimental_Course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `class_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `class_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `participants` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Usage_of_Equipment` (\n  `usage_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_purpose` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`usage_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Usage_of_Equipment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `Experimental_Equipment` (`device_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Usage_of_Equipment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Purchase_Consumables` (\n  `purchase_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `consumable_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`purchase_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Purchase_Consumables_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`consumable_id`) REFERENCES `Experimental_Consumables` (`consumable_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Purchase_Consumables_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Purchase_Hazardous_Chemicals` (\n  `purchase_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `chemical_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `purchase_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`purchase_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Purchase_Hazardous_Chemicals_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`chemical_id`) REFERENCES `Hazardous_Chemicals` (`chemical_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Purchase_Hazardous_Chemicals_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Participation_in_Course` (\n  `participation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `experimental_course_grade` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `participation_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`participation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Participation_in_Course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `Experimental_Course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_Participation_in_Course_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
